macos_platform_tests
  issue 1059
  purpose "The tests worth running on macOS: the ones whose behaviour can differ from Linux."
  rationale "No code in src/ branches on macOS versus Linux -- all eight conditionals are cfg(unix), true on both -- so pure Rust logic cannot behave differently. Every macOS-only failure this repository has recorded came from the environment instead: GNU coreutils absent (timeout), bash 3.2 lacking mapfile, subprocess and path handling."
  cost "Running the whole suite there moved 916MB to each of eight slices, 7GB per run, and two slices of run 32706091539 could not finish that transfer in three attempts while six did it in 20-81s."
  extend "When something behaves differently on macOS, add its module here rather than widening the filter back to everything."

